Text: algeria with the second highest covid-19 cases in africa set up a call centre in the capital algiers on 26 february a day after it confirmed the first case of the virus to boost early detection and help contain wider spread of the disease. around 10 days after being established more than 46 000 people had called the centres 24-hour toll free number. amid answering dozens of calls dr bahia bousri explains that she mainly provides callers with information about the disease and if there is. 
