Text: march 31 2020 the fda says hospitals may get creative if they get overwhelmed with covid-19 patients who need lifesaving ventilators. agency officials on friday issued an emergency use authorization that lets doctors consider attaching the breathing machines to more than one person at a time. the fda also says devices like anesthesia gas machines may be modified so they can be used as ventilators. the new york times reports that one new york city medical center -- new york presbyterian --. 
Answer:

generated_pred:
{
  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "The FDA and agency officials are framed as authoritative problem-solvers preserving public safety by issuing an emergency use authorization and guidance (\"the fda says... issued an emergency use authorization\") and doctors/hospitals are positioned as responders who can \"get creative\" to save lives—functions typical of Guardians/Peacemakers maintaining social order and health."
  },
  "Altruistic_Catalysts": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The text does not depict rebels, martyrs, or underdogs challenging the status quo or sacrificing themselves for systemic change; it focuses on regulatory action and medical responses."
  },
  "Overt_Aggressors": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "There is no language of violence, coercion, or intentional harm; no actors are presented as initiators of conflict or oppression."
  },
  "Deceptive_Subversives": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The passage contains no suggestions of secrecy, betrayal, espionage, or deliberate misinformation—rather it reports transparent regulatory guidance."
  },
  "Institutional_Toxins": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The FDA and hospitals are presented as taking corrective/authoritative action, not as corrupt or incompetent institutions causing harm."
  },
  "Marginalized_Sufferers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "COVID-19 patients are framed as people in need of \"lifesaving ventilators,\" i.e., passive sufferers or victims of a medical crisis whose needs motivate emergency measures."
  }
}

