Text: man who reads nothing at all is better educated than man who reads nothing but newspapers. thomas jefferson editors note after review we are retracting this article. in light of interpretation of this new york times article by health feedback article has been ruled as false misleading. we regret convenience to our readers. new york times just reported something incredible. you know those standard pcr tests for covid-19 virus that everybody in america ha. 
Answer:

generated_pred:
{
  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "An editorial voice and the fact-checker (Health Feedback) are presented as correcting the record: language like 'editors note', 'we are retracting this article', 'ruled as false misleading', and 'we regret' frames these actors as upholding standards and restoring truth."
  },
  "Altruistic_Catalysts": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The text contains no portrayal of rebels, martyrs, or underdogs challenging the status quo or sacrificing for change."
  },
  "Overt_Aggressors": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "There is no depiction of actors initiating violence, oppression, or overt hostility; the content centers on reporting and retraction, not aggression."
  },
  "Deceptive_Subversives": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "A published report (New York Times article) is characterized as having presented misleading information—phrases like 'ruled as false misleading' and 'just reported something incredible' cast the original reporting as deceptive or misinformation."
  },
  "Institutional_Toxins": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "Although an article is retracted, the text frames this as correction rather than explicitly calling the institution corrupt or incompetent; there is no clear depiction of systemic vice or incapacity."
  },
  "Marginalized_Sufferers": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The passage does not portray any group or individual as passive victims, exploited, forgotten, or scapegoated by systemic forces."
  }
}

