Text: immunization services have been disrupted significantly during the covid-19 pandemic threatening the achievements in the eradication and elimination of major vaccine preventable diseases vpds like polio and measles. more than 80 million children under the age of one are estimated to be affected by disruptions in routine immunization services in more than 68 countries and are at risk of polio measles diphtheria pertussis tetanus hepatitis b hemophilus influenza type b pneumococcus and. 
Answer:

generated_pred:
{
  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "Immunization services are framed as protectors of public health—they ‘have been disrupted’ and this disruption is said to be ‘threatening the achievements in the eradication and elimination of major vaccine preventable diseases,’ which positions vaccination programs as guardians of community safety and disease control."
  },
  "Altruistic_Catalysts": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The text does not portray any actors as challengers, rebels, martyrs, or underdogs driving change or sacrifice."
  },
  "Overt_Aggressors": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "There is no language identifying an initiator of conflict, violence, or deliberate harm (tyrant, instigator, terrorist, or bigot). Disruption is attributed to the pandemic, not to a hostile agent."
  },
  "Deceptive_Subversives": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The passage contains no suggestions of secrecy, betrayal, espionage, manipulation, or deliberate deception undermining trust."
  },
  "Institutional_Toxins": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "While services are described as disrupted, the text does not attribute the failure to corruption or incompetence within institutions; the disruption is linked to the COVID-19 pandemic rather than institutional vice."
  },
  "Marginalized_Sufferers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "Children are explicitly cast as passive victims: 'more than 80 million children under the age of one are estimated to be affected' and 'are at risk' of numerous vaccine-preventable diseases, framing them as suffering and vulnerable due to the disruption."
  }
}

