    "explanation": "If Yes, provide evidence of how a participant is framed as a passive sufferer of circumstances (e.g., Victim, Exploited, Forgotten, Scapegoat)."
  }}
}}

Text: a successful case interview allows for the collection of critical information about a person patient diagnosed with covid-19 and potentially exposed contacts while providing support referrals and answers to questions the patient may have. the goals of the case interview are to assess the patients medical condition gather information for continued monitoring and support and obtain the names and location information of their close contacts who may have been exposed to covid-19. developing. 
Answer:

generated_pred:
{
  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "The text frames the case interview process (public health staff) as a protective, stabilizing activity: collecting critical information, providing support referrals, answering questions, assessing medical condition, and gathering contacts for continued monitoring. Language like 'providing support referrals' and goals to 'assess... and support' casts the actors as guardians of public health and safety."
  },
  "Altruistic_Catalysts": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The text does not describe challengers to the status quo, sacrifices for systemic change, or underdog/rebel narratives—only routine public-health procedures."
  },
  "Overt_Aggressors": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "There is no language of violence, domination, instigation, or discriminatory hostility; the passage is procedural and non‑antagonistic."
  },
  "Deceptive_Subversives": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The passage contains no suggestion of secrecy, betrayal, manipulation, or covert activity; it describes transparent data collection and support."
  },
  "Institutional_Toxins": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "Nothing in the text portrays corruption, incompetence, or systemic failure—rather it outlines intended, functional public‑health goals."
  },
  "Marginalized_Sufferers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "The person is presented as a 'patient diagnosed with covid-19' who may need support and whose contacts may have been exposed—portrayed as a passive sufferer/victim of illness who receives referrals and monitoring."
  }
}

