Text: donald trump 11:23 thank you very much everyone. before i begin i d like to offer my condolences and best wishes to the people all across our great south who have endured deadly tornadoes and other severe weather in texas louisiana mississippi alabama florida georgia tennessee and south carolina. donald trump 11:42 my administration will do everything possible to help those communities get back on their feet. were speaking with their governors and representatives. femas alr. 
Answer:

generated_pred:
{
  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "The speaker (the administration) is framed as a protector/guardian: offering condolences and promising assistance—\"my administration will do everything possible to help those communities get back on their feet,\" and coordinating with governors, representatives, and FEMA to restore safety and order."
  },
  "Altruistic_Catalysts": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The text does not portray anyone challenging the status quo, making sacrifices for systemic change, or fighting oppression; it is focused on relief and support after a disaster rather than activism or rebellion."
  },
  "Overt_Aggressors": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "There is no language depicting an initiator of conflict, violence, or oppression; the passage addresses victims of natural disasters and offers help."
  },
  "Deceptive_Subversives": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The excerpt contains no insinuation of secrecy, betrayal, manipulation, espionage, or deceitful actors operating behind the scenes."
  },
  "Institutional_Toxins": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "Although FEMA is mentioned, there is no framing of institutional corruption or incompetence; the administration presents coordination with agencies as part of the response."
  },
  "Marginalized_Sufferers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "Residents of the southern states are framed as victims of deadly tornadoes and severe weather—\"people all across our great south who have endured deadly tornadoes\"—positioning them as passive sufferers in need of aid."
  }
}

